+{"sections":[{"topic":"authority","conclusion":"The authority system enforces strict ownership boundaries by loading fresh AgentDirectory snapshots for each decision and requiring direct ownership relationships. Permissions are checked through AgentToolAuthority which validates caller binding and descendant authorization using the same fresh Directory snapshot. Workspace versions and history inheritance are enforced through the AgentDirectoryReader and require_identifier validation.","evidence":[{"path":"src/traceh/supervision/authority.py","start_line":45,"end_line":50},{"path":"src/traceh/supervision/delegation.py","start_line":128,"end_line":132}]},{"topic":"budget","conclusion":"Subtask budgets are reserved before creation through the reserve_child method, ensuring capacity is available before any work begins. The main agent reserves closing budget by checking for pending reservations in close_account before allowing account closure. Budget enforcement uses ledger.ensure_reservation_capacity and ledger.ensure_charge_capacity to validate capacity before operations.","evidence":[{"path":"src/traceh/budgets/service.py","start_line":107,"end_line":119},{"path":"src/traceh/budgets/service.py","start_line":265,"end_line":272}]},{"topic":"lifecycle","conclusion":"The lifecycle system ensures no running work remains through coordinated admission leases, disposal scopes, and quiescence barriers. Creation/cancellation is handled through the admission context manager and disposal scope registration. Cleanup on failure and main agent termination use wait_quiescent methods to ensure all admitted work completes before shutdown. Products are captured through the event-based ledger system with explicit commit operations.","evidence":[{"path":"src/traceh/supervision/lifecycle.py","start_line":147,"end_line":157},{"path":"src/traceh/supervision/delivery.py","start_line":115,"end_line":124}]}]}
